<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
        The debug build keeps its files apart from the release build's, as it
        keeps its package, its settings and its storage permission apart.

        It has to. The two are different packages and so different uids, and
        scoped storage hands an app only the files it wrote itself: pointed at
        one folder, whichever installed second sees an empty one it cannot even
        write into, because the names it wants are taken by files it is not
        allowed to see. That reads as "ROMs needed" on a machine where the
        release build ran first, and nothing says why.

        No space in the name, deliberately: every adb command, script and doc
        that names the folder would need quoting, and one that forgot would list
        the release build's folder instead and look like it had worked.
    -->
    <string name="data_folder" translatable="false">Zedex-debug</string>

    <!--
        And its name in the launcher, for the same reason one step further
        out: the debug build installs beside the release one rather than over
        it, so both icons sit there together, and two called Zedex is a coin
        toss every time. This is the name of the app everywhere it appears -
        the launcher, the task switcher, the About screen - since app_name is
        one string and all of them read it.

        A space here, unlike data_folder, which must not have one: nothing
        quotes this at a shell prompt, and "Zedex-debug" in a launcher would
        only look like a typo.

        Not translated, because app_name is not: it is a product name and
        values/ holds the only copy, so this override covers every language
        by covering the one string there is.
    -->
    <string name="app_name" translatable="false">Zedex debug</string>
</resources>
